/jerry-rice","teamIds":[14,30,31]},{"id":"walter-payton","name":"Walter Payton","category":"Players","role":"RB","team":"Chicago Bears","classYear":1993,"headline":"Sweetness. Strength. Staying power.","stats":{"rushYards":16726,"rushTD":110,"receptions":492,"Pro Bowls":9},"achievements":["1977 NFL MVP","Super Bowl XX champion","NFL 100 All-Time Team"],"bio":"Payton powered Chicago with a blend of balance, durability and all-purpose skill. His impact reached beyond rushing to receiving, blocking and leadership.","image":"assets/legends/walter-payton.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/walter-payton","teamIds":[20]},{"id":"lawrence-taylor","name":"Lawrence Taylor","category":"Players","role":"LB","team":"New York Giants","classYear":1999,"headline":"The edge that changed the game.","stats":{"sacks":132.5,"defInterceptions":9,"Pro Bowls":10,"Seasons":13},"achievements":["1986 NFL MVP","3\u00d7 NFL Defensive Player of the Year","2\u00d7 Super Bowl champion"],"bio":"Taylor forced offenses to rethink protection. His speed and power helped turn the outside linebacker into an attacking focal point. Sack total covers the official-stat era from 1982.","image":"assets/legends/lawrence-taylor.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/lawrence-taylor","teamIds":[17]},{"id":"joe-montana","name":"Joe Montana","category":"Players","role":"QB","team":"49ers \u00b7 Chiefs","classYear":2000,"headline":"Calm when the stakes were highest.","stats":{"passYards":40551,"passTD":273,"completions":3409,"Pro Bowls":8},"achievements":["4\u00d7 Super Bowl champion","3\u00d7 Super Bowl MVP","2\u00d7 NFL MVP"],"bio":"Montana directed a precise passing attack and delivered memorable late-game drives. His career linked the rise of the West Coast offense with championship execution.","image":"assets/legends/joe-montana.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/joe-montana","teamIds":[13,30]},{"id":"emmitt-smith","name":"Emmitt Smith","category":"Players","role":"RB","team":"Cowboys \u00b7 Cardinals","classYear":2010,"headline":"The long road to the rushing summit.","stats":{"rushYards":18355,"rushTD":164,"receptions":515,"Pro Bowls":8},"achievements":["3\u00d7 Super Bowl champion","1993 NFL MVP","Super Bowl XXVIII MVP"],"bio":"Smith supplied sustained production at the heart of the Dallas dynasty. His patience, vision and durability carried him to the top of the career rushing record book.","image":"assets/legends/emmitt-smith.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/emmitt-smith","teamIds":[16,28]},{"id":"jim-brown","name":"Jim Brown","category":"Players","role":"RB","team":"Cleveland Browns","classYear":1971,"headline":"Nine seasons. An enduring benchmark.","stats":{"rushYards":12312,"rushTD":106,"receptions":262,"Pro Bowls":9},"achievements":["8\u00d7 NFL rushing champion","1964 NFL champion","NFL 100 All-Time Team"],"bio":"Brown dominated an era with power and acceleration. He left football after nine seasons with rushing records that set the target for the runners who followed.","image":"assets/legends/jim-brown.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/jim-brown","teamIds":[6]},{"id":"peyton-manning","name":"Peyton Manning","category":"Players","role":"QB","team":"Colts \u00b7 Broncos","classYear":2021,"headline":"A master of the line of scrimmage.","stats":{"passYards":71940,"passTD":539,"completions":6125,"Pro Bowls":14},"achievements":["5\u00d7 AP NFL MVP","2\u00d7 Super Bowl champion","Super Bowl XLI MVP"],"bio":"Manning made pre-snap command a defining part of quarterback play. He led championship teams in Indianapolis and Denver over an 18-season playing career.","image":"assets/legends/peyton-manning.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/peyton-manning","teamIds":[9,12]},{"id":"barry-sanders","name":"Barry Sanders","category":"Players","role":"RB","team":"Detroit Lions","classYear":2004,"headline":"A cut could change everything.","stats":{"rushYards":15269,"rushTD":99,"Pro Bowls":10,"Seasons":10},"achievements":["1997 NFL MVP","4\u00d7 NFL rushing champion","2,053 rushing yards in 1997"],"bio":"Sanders turned balance and sudden changes of direction into an unmistakable style. He rushed for at least 1,000 yards in every season of his ten-year career.","image":"assets/legends/barry-sanders.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/barry-sanders","teamIds":[21]},{"id":"reggie-white","name":"Reggie White","category":"Players","role":"DE","team":"Eagles \u00b7 Packers \u00b7 Panthers","classYear":2006,"headline":"Power at the point of attack.","stats":{"Pro Bowls":13,"10+ sack seasons":12,"Eagles sacks":124,"Packers sacks":68.5},"achievements":["Super Bowl XXXI champion","NFL 100 All-Time Team","10\u00d7 first-team All-Pro"],"bio":"White combined strength with refined pass-rush technique. He anchored formidable fronts in Philadelphia and Green Bay and helped the Packers return to a championship.","image":"assets/legends/reggie-white.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/reggie-white","teamIds":[18,22,25]},{"id":"bill-walsh","name":"Bill Walsh","category":"Coaches","role":"Head coach","team":"San Francisco 49ers","classYear":1993,"headline":"An idea became an offensive language.","stats":{"Overall wins":102,"Overall losses":63,"Overall ties":1,"Super Bowl titles":3},"achievements":["Super Bowls XVI, XIX & XXIII","1981 NFL Coach of the Year","6 division championships"],"bio":"Walsh built a championship program through teaching, player evaluation and a structured passing system. His coaching influence extended through generations of assistants.","image":"assets/legends/bill-walsh.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/bill-walsh","teamIds":[30]},{"id":"john-madden","name":"John Madden","category":"Coaches","role":"Head coach \u00b7 Broadcaster","team":"Oakland Raiders","classYear":2006,"headline":"A teacher who brought football closer.","stats":{"Regular-season wins":103,"Regular-season losses":32,"Regular-season ties":7,"Losing seasons":0},"achievements":["Super Bowl XI champion","8 playoff appearances in 10 seasons","1969 AFL Coach of the Year"],"bio":"Madden led consistently successful Raiders teams before becoming a defining football broadcaster. His teaching connected the detail of the game with a broad audience.","image":"assets/legends/john-madden.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/john-madden","teamIds":[14]},{"id":"don-shula","name":"Don Shula","category":"Coaches","role":"Head coach","team":"Colts \u00b7 Dolphins","classYear":1997,"headline":"Consistency measured in decades.","stats":{"Overall wins":347,"Overall losses":173,"Overall ties":6,"Seasons":33},"achievements":["2\u00d7 Super Bowl champion","1972 perfect 17\u20130 season","20 postseason appearances"],"bio":"Shula built winning teams across changing eras. His Miami program delivered consecutive championships and the unbeaten 1972 season.","image":"assets/legends/don-shula.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/don-shula","teamIds":[1,9]},{"id":"george-halas","name":"George Halas","category":"Founders","role":"Founder \u00b7 Owner \u00b7 Head coach","team":"Chicago Bears","classYear":1963,"headline":"At the foundations of the league.","stats":{"Coaching wins":324,"Coaching seasons":40,"NFL titles as coach":6,"Playing seasons":9},"achievements":["Charter Hall of Fame class","Founded the Decatur Staleys","Attended the 1920 league organizational meeting"],"bio":"Halas helped establish the league and the franchise that became the Chicago Bears. His career spanned playing, coaching, ownership and football administration.","image":"assets/legends/george-halas.webp","source":"https://www.profootballhof.com/players/george-halas","teamIds":[20]},{"id":"jim-kelly","name":"Jim Kelly","category":"Players","role":"QB","team":"Buffalo Bills","teamIds":[0],"classYear":2002,"headline":"A name woven into franchise history.","bio":"Jim Kelly is part of Buffal